From: steamac <steamac@fxgam.es>
Subject: [PATCH] kk: reject incompatible color view block sizes before Metal

STEAMAC-3 d7f4d319 is a different assertion from the zero-slice events:
Metal rejects an RGBA8Unorm source viewed as R8Unorm. Reject incompatible
color texel block sizes at vkCreateImageView before asking Metal, whose
validation aborts the host rather than returning nil. Do not compare the
combined sizes for depth/stencil or multi-planar aspect views. Compressed
block-texel aliases retain their equal-sized blocks and existing alias path.
Log both Vulkan formats and image flags/usage on rejection.

Repro: image_views.c invalid-format-2d reproduces the precise RGBA8 -> R8
assert under Metal API validation on M1 Max.

Generated-by: LLM
---
--- a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_image_view.c
+++ b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_image_view.c
@@ -86,6 +86,23 @@
                        (unsigned long long)image->vk.usage, image->vk.tiling);
    }
 
+   /* A mutable color format still needs the same texel block size. In
+    * particular RGBA8 -> R8 is not a Metal pixel-format view, and aborts
+    * instead of returning nil. Depth/stencil and multi-planar aspect views
+    * select their actual plane format below and must not use this test. */
+   const VkFormat format = pCreateInfo->format == VK_FORMAT_UNDEFINED
+                              ? image->vk.format : pCreateInfo->format;
+   if (image->plane_count == 1 &&
+       range->aspectMask == VK_IMAGE_ASPECT_COLOR_BIT &&
+       vk_format_get_blocksize(format) !=
+          vk_format_get_blocksize(image->vk.format)) {
+      return vk_errorf(dev, VK_ERROR_FORMAT_NOT_SUPPORTED,
+                       "kk: incompatible image view format %u for image "
+                       "format %u, type %u, flags 0x%llx, usage 0x%llx",
+                       format, image->vk.format, pCreateInfo->viewType,
+                       (unsigned long long)image->vk.create_flags,
+                       (unsigned long long)image->vk.usage);
+   }
 
    memset(view, 0, sizeof(*view));
 
